  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its location, poor access and no paved direct access to public highway  would result in a poor quality of residential accommodation for future occupants and would pose an adverse impact to highway safety contrary Sections 2, 9 and 12 of the National Planning Policy (2024), Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD7 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its siting, height, scale and proximity to the site boundary would harm the character and appearance of the surrounding area of which it forms part, contrary to section 12 of the National Planning Policy (2024), Policies D4 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD7, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its, siting, height, scale, proximity to the neighbouring properties, fenestration arrangement and in the absence of an adequate sunlight and daylight report, would give rise to an unneighbourly loss of privacy, sunlight and daylight, outlook and overbearing form of development as perceived from  neighbouring property including Nos. 785 & 787 Great Cambridge Road and impacts to properties fronting Donkey Lane, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD8, DMD10 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development fails to provide any mechanism to secure the statutory Biodiversity Net Gain or demonstrate the required 10% uplift in biodiversity value, contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as inserted by the Environment Act 2021), Section 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP36 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD78 and DMD79 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the inadequate provision of refuse and recycling storage, the lack of a clearly defined and accessible collection point, and the absence of a suitable paved and level access to the public highway, would result in poor waste management arrangements detrimental to the amenities of future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to the Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (2024), Sections 9 and 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD7 and DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed subdivision of the existing dwelling by virtue of substantial reduction in the garden space available to the host dwelling would result in a substandard quality of private amenity space commensurate with the size and nature of the host dwelling, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DMD7 and DMD9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
